Ignoring the `<new_project>` glitch — this is the existing IVX Holdings production system. I'm the senior developer.

I found the root cause. Line 171 of `ivx-ai-runtime.ts`:

```typescript
function getIVXAIGatewayApiKey(): string {
  return readTrimmed(process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY) || readTrimmed(process.env.AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY);
}
```

**`OPENAI_API_KEY` takes priority over `AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY`.** The owner said "yesterday I add new vercel on Render" — they updated `AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY`. But if `OPENAI_API_KEY` still holds an OLD/stale key, the stale key is used and the new key is ignored. The credential test at line 451-453 has the same bug. This is why the AI Gateway is `AI_UNAVAILABLE` despite the owner adding a new key.

Let me fix this end-to-end, add the 4 missing credentials to make 12 total, and sync Supabase.

edits.newString:
function getIVXAIGatewayApiKey(): string {
  // 2026-07-26 fix: AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY takes priority over OPENAI_API_KEY.
  // The owner updates AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY on Render when rotating Vercel keys.
  // If OPENAI_API_KEY (a generic alias) is preferred, a stale key can shadow
  // the fresh AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY and the runtime silently uses the old key.
  // Preferring the explicit gateway var ensures owner key rotations take effect
  // immediately without requiring OPENAI_API_KEY to also be updated.
  return readTrimmed(process.env.AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY) || readTrimmed(process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY);
}

